<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Multan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Multan is an ancient city in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> captured it in 1818, extending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>. A revolt at Multan in 1848 sparked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-sikh-war">Second Anglo-Sikh War</a>, which ended with the British annexation of the Punjab.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/multan.jpg" alt="Multan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yaarahmadd · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shrine_Shah_Rukn-e-Alam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
